  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/ogham/dog/zipball/v0.1.0",
  "body": "This is the first public release of [dog](https://dns.lookup.dog)! At this point, it has the following features:\r\n\r\n- Runs on Windows, macOS, and Linux\r\n- Understands sixteen record types: `A`, `AAAA`, `CAA`, `CNAME`, `HINFO`, `LOC`, `MX`, `NAPTR`, `NS`, `OPT`, `PTR`, `SOA`, `SRV`, `SSHFP`, `TLSA`, and `TXT`\r\n- Can use the UDP, TCP, DNS-over-TLS, and DNS-over-HTTPS network transports\r\n\r\nThe releases are signed using [minisign](https://jedisct1.github.io/minisign/). The public key is available on [my website](https://bsago.me/contact). I just realised I should make it available over DNS somehow.\r\n\r\n![Screenshot 2020-11-07 at 12 39 27](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/503760/98441447-482ec380-20f6-11eb-8b6f-8c25368b661f.png)\r\n",
